# Local scratch diagnostics (never commit; may contain local device paths)
scratch_*.py

# Deliberately NO ignore rule for other agent CLIs' config dirs. Naming one here reintroduces
# the very token P18 bans, because .gitignore is itself tracked content — an ignore rule has to
# spell out what it excludes, so the rule and the brand lock cannot both hold. Adding one failed
# `test_no_legacy_ose_opencode_tokens_reappear` on 2026-07-31. The path guard beside it
# (`test_no_legacy_tokens_in_tracked_paths`) is the stronger check anyway: it fails the suite if
# such a directory is ever staged, where an ignore rule only shields it from `git add -A`.

# Secrets / local env overrides (use ~/.config/rag-search/env instead)
.env
